     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, can someone briefly explain what &quot;<a href=\"http://std.lv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423195747000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1FTE9kFB72B1fMOwN5wk9M\">std.lv</a>&quot; in sem() do? I have read the two sentences of explanation here <a href=\"http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/syntax2.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/syntax2.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423195747000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Gc1d6KIkfPY3wUMslNg0c\">http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/syntax2.html</a> but it is still not clear. <div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "mKdZfmrcAQAJ",
   "from": "Edward Rigdon",
   "author": "99a06696c483481a",
   "date": "2019-08-13T20:00:37Z",
   "subject": "Re: std.lv",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">It fixes the variances of all common factor to be equal to 1. So instead of constraining loadings to achieve identification, you have constrained factor variances. For somepeople, it eases interpretation, as well.<div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
